          "guid": "mspkb7h9dvmxhh1v",
          "message": {
            "text": "Literal NUL source bytes made the paired oracle's import graph platform-parser-dependent. Escaped backslash-zero spellings preserve every runtime cache-key separator while keeping TypeScript portable; the fixture unit test now scans all production TypeScript under src and tools so CI catches the entire class before native Windows.",
            "markdown": "Literal NUL source bytes made the paired oracle's import graph platform-parser-dependent. Escaped backslash-zero spellings preserve every runtime cache-key separator while keeping TypeScript portable; the fixture unit test now scans all production TypeScript under src and tools so CI catches the entire class before native Windows."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "tools/shaping-conformance.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 689,
                  "endLine": 715,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "    const allow: Set<string> = existsSync(opts.allowlistFile)\n      ? new Set((JSON.parse(readFileSync(opts.allowlistFile, \"utf-8\")) as Array<{ text: string; fontFamily: string }>)\n        .map((e) => `${e.text}\\0${e.fontFamily}`))\n      : new Set();\n\n    const ctx = await browser.newContext({ viewport: { width: 1400, height: 900 } });\n    const page = await ctx.newPage();\n\n    const counts: Record<Verdict, number> = {\n      \"agree-exact\": 0, \"agree-count\": 0, \"agree-count-clustered\": 0,\n      \"mismatch-count\": 0, \"mismatch-unrendered\": 0,\n    };\n    const rows: MismatchRow[] = [];\n    const routes = new Map<string, number>();\n    let allowlisted = 0;\n    const posDeltas: number[] = [];\n    const t0 = Date.now();\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < runs.length; i += opts.batch) {\n      const batch = runs.slice(i, i + opts.batch);\n      const chrome = await chromeShaping(page, batch);\n      for (let j = 0; j < batch.length; j++) {\n        const spec = batch[j];\n        const ours = ourShaping(spec);\n        const { verdict, maxDelta } = compareShaping(chrome[j], ours, opts.tolerance);\n        if (verdict.startsWith(\"mismatch\") && allow.has(`${spec.text}\\0${spec.fontFamily}`)) {\n          allowlisted++;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
